  "scope_notes": [
    "222 is the Swift Testing target total, including legacy PrototypeDeletionTests; legacy passes are not acceptance evidence for the current amount model.",
    "The acceptance UI run selected only NativePortUITests: 10 tests passed. Historical four-tab UI tests were not fully migrated or run as an entire UI regression.",
    "UI tests launch -design-preview with isolated sample SwiftData; native save/confirm/result paths are exercised, not a user ledger or live cloud provider.",
    "The wish purchase UI test begins at the redemption form and verifies explicit purchase confirmation, result and return; its name alone does not prove a flip gesture.",
    "Small-screen run uses English, dark mode, AccessibilityXXXL and reduced motion. This is one representative path, not all screens at every size.",
    "VoiceOver automation on iOS 27 verifies budget amount and holder-library action reachability; it is not an all-screen spoken audit.",
    "iPad initial cover flow failed to find native.cover.open. After stable large-detent adaptation for regular width, the same cover flow passed; the earlier failure remains reported.",
    "An intermediate 10-test polish run failed two tests: an ambiguous task-menu query and detail opening during holder layer return. Menu targeting, layer-return detail gating and readiness checks were corrected; the acceptance run passed all 10.",
    "The added expanded-wish UI path actually taps the card to reveal Redeem, confirms purchase, closes the result and verifies the realized tab. Reduced-motion large-text path checks Fill Price is hittable, rather than mere accessibility-tree existence.",
    "Final 375pt screenshot files use native-se-*.png, 750x1334 pixels, from the small-navigation-acceptance run. Older iPhone 18 Pro screenshots named native-small-dark-large-* were removed, not presented as SE evidence.",
    "Bottom navigation text is locally capped at xxxLarge with controlled scaling on small devices; other content uses the requested AccessibilityXXXL, and full VoiceOver labels remain available.",
    "The last change after the 222-test and 10-test runs is a rounded Canvas clip only. Simulator and Release builds and final code-signature checks passed afterward; the test suites were not rerun after that final rendering patch."
  ],
